{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455504-dei-enhancement-enlightenent-dice","id":1455504,"title":"DEI enhancement Enlightenent dice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-24T05:14:54-07:00","id":1455504,"title":"DEI enhancement Enlightenent dice?","content":"In M20 Technocracy Reloaded, the DEI is considered an Enhancement (page 186), but shouldn\u2019t it have an Enlightenment rating? It can run ES-phone apps (page 180) and PPP (page 175), but I don't see anywhere that indicates how many Enlightenment dice are rolled to activate them, or enter the Digital Web with the inherent Data2 effect that the DEI has. The ES-phone, being a Device (Wonder) has an Enlightenment of 3-6, so should I assume the DEI has an Enlightenment of 6?<br /> <br /> How many dice would you have someone with a DEI Enhancement roll to activate an ES-phone app?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> The more I think about this, the more I think the DEI should be considered an implanted version of the ES-phone, bought with the Enhancements background and costing a base of 4 background points. So something like:<br /> Enlightenment 3, Primal Energy 15 costs 4 background points<br /> Enlightenment 4, Primal Energy 20 costs 6 background points<br /> Enlightenment 5, Primal Energy 25 costs 8 background points<br /> Enlightenment 6, Primal Energy 30 costs 10 background points<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 07-24-2021, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custo